BT /F1 10.0 Tf 48.00 317.00 Td (Subwords are mean-pooled into the whitespace token they overlap most. An equal overlap stays on the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 48.00 304.00 Td (earlier token. A whitespace token with no subword becomes a zero vector. Its cosine is defined as 0, so) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 48.00 291.00 Td (its score is 1. After the windows of one side are stitched, each token is scored against the other) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 48.00 278.00 Td (side's full sequence. The written score is clamp\(1 - max cosine, 0, 1\), rounded to 6 decimals.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 48.00 261.00 Td (The paper's DiffAlign takes the final hidden state and does not clamp, so a negative cosine can score) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 48.00 248.00 Td (above 1. SpanDiff clamps. The final-layer row in the table is the clamped version of that recipe on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 48.00 235.00 Td (this 8B model. An unclamped rescore of the saved final-layer states was not produced. The paper also) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 48.00 222.00 Td (takes the maximum at subword level and then averages inside the word. SpanDiff pools the states first) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 48.00 209.00 Td (and then takes the maximum. The graded files keep that order.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 48.00 192.00 Td (Encoder lines contain only id, text_a, text_b, labels_a, and labels_b. Every label is in [0, 1]. The) Tj ET
